 "notes": [
  "The students in the Computer Engineering BS degree program are required to take several courses taught by the Computer Science Department. Those classes are: COMP163 Introduction to Computer Programming; COMP 167 Computer Program Design; COMP 280 Data Structures; COMP 285 Design and Analysis of Algorithms; and COMP 350 Operating Systems. It is the Computer Science department\u2019s policy that all prerequisite courses must be completed with a \u201cC\u201d or better. All of the classes above, except COMP 350, are prerequisite courses and therefore require a \u201cC\u201d grade to satisfy the prerequisite requirement."
